    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n\n- **`buildCustomerCode`** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:202`) now takes the city and last name. It builds `CITY3` from the upper-cased first three letters of the city, `LAST3` from the last name, and `NNNN` as a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already in that city (case-insensitive match), instead of the previous global owner count.\n- Updated the call site (`:134`) to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\nEverything derived from `customerCode` rebuilds automatically: the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is computed as `customerCode + \"-M\" + <2-digit year>`, so it now reflects the new format without further changes.\n\nNo seed-data or schema changes were needed \u2014 the seed inserts leave `customer_code` null (it's only assigned on creation), and the new 12-char value fits the existing `VARCHAR(20)` column.\n\nThe test suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance check confirms the customer code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`.",
